    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "A calibrated drop-and-bounce lab in a stationary synthetic medium. Gravity, ball mass/radius and surface restitution are known. F_drag = -b(z) * velocity in all components, with z the sphere-centre height above the floor. The invisible coefficient b(z) is a fixed, nonnegative, continuously varying function of height, not restricted to two constant layers. It does not change between experiments. Infer an approximate profile from timed drops and rebounds. No buoyancy, spin, tangential contact friction or object-object collisions are modeled. Only instrument readings are available, not trajectories or direct coefficient measurements.\nUse submit_action: inspect, drop, or bounce. Drop and bounce require specimen_id and release_height_m; bounce also requires surface_id. Valid measurements share a budget; invalid actions, inspection and submissions are free. Submit your approximate function with operation submit_drag_estimate, heights_m and coefficients_kg_s arrays, using the public interpolation rule. The samples are your chosen approximation, not a request for the private grid. Function heights refer to sphere centres above the floor, while release and rebound heights are bottom clearances. Your profile will be assessed by how well it predicts impact times and rebound heights at additional release heights; an exact parameter match is not required. Submissions only acknowledge receipt and provide no correctness feedback. Explain the experiments supporting your conclusion, then call finish.\nInitial observation:\n{\n  \"specimens\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"sample_A\",\n      \"color\": \"blue\",\n      \"shape\": \"sphere\",\n      \"mass_kg\": 0.1,\n      \"radius_m\": 0.030000000000000006\n    }\n  ],\n  \"calibration\": {\n    \"gravity_m_s2\": 3.0,\n    \"surface_id\": \"surface_1\",\n    \"restitution\": 0.8\n  },\n  \"profile_family\": {\n    \"type\": \"unknown_smooth_height_function\",\n    \"coefficient_bounds_kg_s\": [\n      0,\n      0.5\n    ],\n    \"height_domain_m\": [\n      0,\n      3\n    ],\n    \"height_reference\": \"sphere centre above floor\",\n    \"stationary\": true,\n    \"outside_domain\": \"constant endpoint values\",\n    \"estimate_representation\": \"Choose 2\\u201365 heights spanning 0 to 3 m and matching coefficients. Between adjacent samples use u=(z-z_i)/(z_next-z_i), w=3*u^2-2*u^3, b(z)=(1-w)*b_i+w*b_next. Minimum sample spacing is 0.01 m. Your sampling grid need not match the hidden function grid.\"\n  },\n  \"apparatus\": {\n    \"min_release_height_m\": 0.05,\n    \"max_release_height_m\": 2.5,\n    \"release_height_reference\": \"bottom-of-sphere clearance above floor\",\n    \"clock_resolution_s\": 0.001,\n    \"height_resolution_m\": 0.001,\n    \"drop_readout\": \"time to first impact\",\n    \"bounce_readout\": \"time to first impact and first rebound bottom clearance\"\n  },\n  \"experiments_used\": 0,\n  \"experiments_remaining\": 24,\n  \"notebook\": []\n}"
    },
